From 1dd36f4f45e3ad8004bd714c1f1b7a61b0f4b28f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 03:25:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(players): decode signed actor IDs in the player list

PlayerListAddEntry uses compressed ActorUniqueID, a signed 64-bit value in the Bedrock 1.26.51 protocol-2193 schema. Decode its ZigZag representation consistently with StartGame instead of retaining the unsigned wire value.

The private protocol-2193 skin relay exposed the mismatch: a spawned actor with ID 1 appeared in PlayerListStorage under ID 2. Live skin changes could not resolve the local UUID, and scoreboard associations could resolve another actor. Gophertunnel emits signed IDs as specified by the native schema.

Evidence: https://github.com/Mojang/bedrock-protocol-docs/blob/v1.26.51/json/PlayerListAddEntry.json and https://github.com/Mojang/bedrock-protocol-docs/blob/v1.26.51/json/ActorUniqueID.json
---
 .../java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/HudPackets.java | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/HudPackets.java b/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/HudPackets.java
index a0824a64..a8564eaf 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/HudPackets.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/HudPackets.java
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@ public final class HudPackets {
                 switch (action) {
                     case Add -> {
                         final UUID uuid = wrapper.read(BedrockTypes.UUID); // uuid
-                        final long entityUniqueId = wrapper.read(BedrockTypes.UNSIGNED_VAR_LONG); // actorUniqueId
+                        final long entityUniqueId = wrapper.read(BedrockTypes.VAR_LONG); // actorUniqueId
                         final String name = wrapper.read(BedrockTypes.STRING); // name
                         final String xuid = wrapper.read(BedrockTypes.STRING); // xuid
                         final String platformOnlineId = wrapper.read(BedrockTypes.STRING); // platform online id
-- 
